course: dictionary
lesson: 14366
title: Opposing: against, or very different
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Opposing means against someone or something, or very different from something else. Context tells you which meaning fits. «The opposing team scored in the last minute.» The opposing team is the team you are playing against, so opposing means the other side in a game.
explain: «Our class had opposing views about the new playground.» Some children wanted a pond and some wanted a climbing frame. Their views were the opposite of each other. Try the swap test: put «different» in place of opposing. If the sentence still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
explain: Opposing can also be a verb, from oppose. «The head teacher is opposing the plan.» Here she is against the plan. The verb changes its form: oppose, opposes, opposed, opposing.
fact: Opposing means being against someone or something, or being very different.
fact: «The opposing team» means the team you are playing against.
fact: «Opposing views» means views that are very different from each other.
fact: In science, opposing forces push in opposite directions.
fact: The verb is oppose: «They oppose the new road», «They are opposing the new road», «They opposed it last year».
exercise: «The opposing team wore red shirts.» What does opposing mean in this sentence? | Friendly, on our side | *The other team, the one you are playing against | Very tired | Lost
exercise: «Mia and Sam had opposing views about pets.» What does opposing mean here? | Quick | The same as each other | Very loud | *Very different from each other
exercise: Which word is the base form of the verb opposing? | *oppose | opposite | opponent | opposing team
test: «The opposing forces pushed in opposite directions.» What does opposing mean here? | Very soft | Lost | *Pushing against each other, in opposite directions | Pushing in the same way
test: «They are opposing the new park.» Which word means the same as opposing in this sentence? | Forgetting | Helping | Agreeing with | *Being against
exam: Complete the sentence: «The ___ views in the debate made it exciting.» | *Opposing | Same | Quiet | Happy
